note dl/dlclone.om: the clone panel of the Radicle-storage build (texts tdcl*, fns dlputrid, dlclone),
note moved out of dl/dl.om unchanged so that the store-reading build can compose store/clone.om in its
note place (run.sh units). It reads dl.om's helpers and texts, so it is composed after dl/dl.om.
text tdcl1 "<div class=\"clone\"><h3>Get this repository</h3><dl><dt>Radicle</dt><dd><code>rad clone rad:"
text tdcl2 "</code></dd><dt>Git over HTTPS</dt><dd><code>git clone https://www.aienos.com/rad/"
text tdcl3 ".git</code></dd><dt>Source archive of "
text tdcl4 "</dt><dd><a href=\""
text tdcl5 ".zip\">zip</a> &middot; <a href=\""
text tdcl6 ".tar.gz\">tar.gz</a></dd></dl></div>\n"
text tdcl7 "<p class=\"meta\">One command for agents: <code>forge-contribute "
text tdcl8 " DIR BRANCH TITLE CMD SUB AGENT REPO FILE BODY DATA HOME</code> clones, branches, commits, opens a Radicle patch with an evidence receipt (exact commit, command, exit status, output sha256) and requests review. Arguments and exit codes: docs/ANNOYANCES.md in interplane-forge.</p>\n"
fn dlputrid to void
for i ulong get fridl 0
fescc get frid i
end
end
fn dlclone to void
dldefbr
fput tdcl1
dlputrid
fput tdcl2
dlputrid
fput tdcl3
dlescref
fput tdcl4
dlrepol
fput tdarhh
dlescref
fput tdcl5
dlrepol
fput tdarhh
dlescref
fput tdcl6
fput tdcl7
dlputrid
fput tdcl8
end
